WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.295
EDR is not only about detection.

2
00:00:02.295 --> 00:00:04.091
It also supports response.

3
00:00:04.091 --> 00:00:18.010
Depending on the tool and permissions, responders may isolate a host from the network, kill a process, quarantine a file, collect forensic data, search for related indicators, or trigger remediation actions.

4
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.281
These capabilities can reduce the time between detection and containment.

5
00:00:22.281 --> 00:00:32.667
If a laptop appears to be spreading malware or connecting to a known command-and-control server, isolation can help prevent additional damage while analysts investigate.

6
00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:39.372
If a suspicious file is found, quarantine can reduce exposure while preserving information for review.

7
00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:41.528
Response actions require judgment.

8
00:00:41.528 --> 00:00:45.369
Isolating a critical server may disrupt business operations.

9
00:00:45.369 --> 00:00:48.023
Killing a process may destroy useful evidence.

10
00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:54.509
A good EDR workflow balances speed, evidence preservation, business impact, and risk reduction.
